# `isPart` is copied in line into the condition of the loop. Three of its returns are quiet; the fourth comes out of `wide` or `older`, which are called. They met behind the copy, in front of the loop's own branch, and behind that meeting nothing was known:
# so no way round was quiet, the loop got no front of quiet turns, and `end` and `text` were read and tested in every turn and `at` was read again behind the meeting.
# The quiet returns walk the end of the block apart from the loud ones; in the last block of the turn they stay apart as they did before. The typed build has a front (which counts as a head) and a head; the written copy has the third.
# RUN: walk f16 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-COUNT-3: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-NOT: isLoopHead=true
# `wide` lays another text, a longer one, a rope, one of wide characters; cuts the end; moves the place; lays a text and a fraction in the place of the end. Each is seen in the very next turn.
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: 162 lines 1610314678
